{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.GeometryOfIncompleteness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.GeometryOfIncompleteness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Information.PhysicalIntractability"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.horizon_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.horizon_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GeometryOfIncompleteness.lean#L117-L127","doc":"**The horizon is nonempty (sorry-free).**  Corollary: under the same\nhypotheses there exists an inaccessible degree-0 datum — the jet horizon\n`Γ(𝓗, A₀) = 0` is realised.  A Turing-complete substrate necessarily hosts\na region where degree-0 truth is inaccessible: the event horizon is the\ngeometry of incompleteness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.geometry_of_incompleteness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.geometry_of_incompleteness","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GeometryOfIncompleteness.lean#L94-L115","doc":"**The geometry of incompleteness (capstone, sorry-free).**  Given\n(i) a Gödel datum that is formally unprovable — the incompleteness witness,\nforced in any Turing-complete substrate — and\n(ii) a boundary datum whose bandwidth-`B` extractor must read the full\n`3^{3n}` surviving resolution tree — the physical witness —\nthe jet horizon is **nonempty**: some degree-0 truth is inaccessible.  The\nboundary datum is inaccessible *physically* (derived via\n`qou_physical_intractability_unconditional`), and the Gödel datum is\ninaccessible *formally*.  Incompleteness and physical intractability are the\ntwo faces of the vanishing of degree-0 sections. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:geometry-of-incompleteness","label":"thm:geometry-of-incompleteness","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/geometry-of-incompleteness.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.not_inaccessible_of_all_provable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.not_inaccessible_of_all_provable","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GeometryOfIncompleteness.lean#L81-L92","doc":"**The notion is refutable**, which it was not while provability was a\nconstructor-chosen field: under a predicate that holds of everything, a\ndatum with a polynomially-bounded extractor is NOT behind the horizon.\n\nPreviously `Inaccessible` could be discharged for a fabricated datum at\nany `FormallyProvable`, so no instance of \"accessible\" existed to exhibit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.inaccessible_of_intractable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.inaccessible_of_intractable","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GeometryOfIncompleteness.lean#L76-L79","doc":"**A physically-intractable datum is behind the horizon (sorry-free).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.inaccessible_of_unprovable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.inaccessible_of_unprovable","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GeometryOfIncompleteness.lean#L71-L74","doc":"**A Gödel-unprovable datum is behind the horizon (sorry-free).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.Inaccessible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.Inaccessible","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GeometryOfIncompleteness.lean#L63-L69","doc":"A datum is **inaccessible** — behind the jet horizon `Γ(𝓗, A₀) = 0` — when\nit is either formally unprovable (Gödel) or physically intractable\n(super-polynomial extraction), with provability judged by the caller's\n`FormallyProvable`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.DegreeZeroDatum.extractSteps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.DegreeZeroDatum.extractSteps","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GeometryOfIncompleteness.lean#L61-L61","doc":"The step-count of a physical extractor (as a function of instance size). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.DegreeZeroDatum.datum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.DegreeZeroDatum.datum","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GeometryOfIncompleteness.lean#L59-L59","doc":"The datum itself — the thing whose provability is at issue. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.DegreeZeroDatum.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.DegreeZeroDatum.mk","kind":"ctor","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GeometryOfIncompleteness.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.DegreeZeroDatum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.DegreeZeroDatum","kind":"structure","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/GeometryOfIncompleteness.lean#L31-L61","doc":"A **degree-0 datum**: a decision answer / particle identity / truth value,\ncarried as an element of a caller-supplied `Datum` type, together with the\nstep-count needed to physically extract it.\n\n**`formallyProvable : Prop` was a field until 2026-09-14 and is now a\ncaller-supplied predicate** (`FormallyProvable : Datum → Prop`, a parameter\nof `Inaccessible` below).  As a field it was typed with the *universe*\n`Prop`, so the CONSTRUCTOR chose the proposition — and that made the\ncapstone dischargeable with no mathematical content.  Verified before the\nchange, not asserted:\n\n```\nexample : ∃ d : DegreeZeroDatum, Inaccessible d :=\n  horizon_nonempty { formallyProvable := False, extractSteps := fun n => n }\n    not_false          -- compiled, exit 0\n```\n\n\"There exists a datum that is not formally provable\" was proved by\n*defining* one whose provability proposition is literally `False`.  The\nstructure also had no datum in it — only a `Prop` and a step-count — so\nthere was nothing for provability to be *about*.\n\nWith `Datum` and `FormallyProvable` supplied by the caller, applying the\ncapstone now requires exhibiting a real carrier and a real failure of\nprovability on it — which is Gödel's theorem, i.e. content.  And it is\nrefutable: see `not_inaccessible_of_all_provable`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}